"hadiths[73]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1468,"Ibn Samura al-'Adawi reported:I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) say, and he then narrated (the above-mentioned hadith)"""
1469,"We took part in the holy battle of Tabuk in the company of the Prophet (ﷺ) and when we arrived at the Wadi-al-Qura, there was a woman in her garden. The Prophet (ﷺ) asked his companions to estimate the amount of the fruits in the garden, and Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) estimated it at ten Awsuq (One Wasaq = 60 Sa's) and 1 Sa'= 3 kg. approximately). The Prophet (ﷺ) said to that lady, Check what your garden will yield."" When we reached Tabuk ""1470"",Jabir reported:We fought In the company of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with the tribe of Juhaina. They fought with us terribly. When we had finished the noon prayer ""1471"",This hadith has been transmitted by Ibrahim b. Sa'd b. Malik on the authority of his father"""
1470,"[AI-translation] From Jabir bin 'Abdullah, who said: We went on an expedition with the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, the expedition of Najd. When the midday rest overtook him while he was in a valley with many thorny trees, he alighted under a tree and sought shade beneath it, and hung his sword. The people dispersed among the trees seeking shade. While we were like that, the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, called us, so we came. Behold, a Bedouin was sitting before him. He said: ""This man came to me while I was asleep, and unsheathed my sword. I woke up while he was standing at my head, holding the sword unsheathed. He said: 'Who will protect you from me?' I said: 'Allah.' So he sheathed it, then sat down, and here he is."" He said: ""And the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, did not punish him.""
1471"""
1471,"Narrated Abu Musa: The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""The example of guidance and knowledge with which Allah has sent me is like abundant rain falling on the earth, some of which was fertile soil that absorbed the water and brought forth grass and abundant vegetation. Some of it was hard and held the water, and Allah benefited the people with it, so they drank from it, gave water to their animals, and irrigated their crops. Another portion of it fell on barren land, which could neither hold the water nor bring forth vegetation. The first is the example of the person who comprehends Allah's religion and benefits from what Allah has sent me with, so he learns and teaches others; and the (last example) is that of the person who does not care for it at all and does not accept Allah's guidance with which I have been sent."" In another narration: ""And a portion of it retained the water (in pools)."""
1472,"Narrated Abu Huraira: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying, ""My similitude and the similitude of mankind is that of a man who kindled a fire, and when it illuminated what was around it, moths and these insects that fall into fire began to fall into it. He tried to drive them away, but they overpowered him and rushed into it. So I am taking hold of your waist-belts to keep you away from the Fire, but you rush into it."""
1473,"A bedouin came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, My wife has delivered a black child."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him"""
1474,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, My similitude in comparison with the other prophets is that of a man who has built a house completely and excellently except for a place of one brick. When the people enter the house"""
1475,"I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) saying, Whoever claims to be the son of a person other than his father"""
1476,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, I am your predecessor (forerunner) at the Lake-Fount ""1477"",They are of me (i.e. my followers). It will be said"""
1477,"[AI-translation] Khudri, who adds in it: ""And I will say: 'They are from me.' It will be said: 'You do not know what they introduced after you.' So I will say: 'Away with them, away with them, to those who altered things after me.'""
1478"""
1478,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr: The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""My Lake-Fount is (so vast that it takes) a month's journey (to cross), its water is whiter than milk, its smell is sweeter than musk, and its drinking cups are like the stars of the sky; whoever drinks from it will never be thirsty again."""
1479,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, I will be standing at the Lake-Fount so that I will see whom among you will come to me; and some people will be taken away from me"""
1480,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) offered the funeral prayers of the martyrs of Uhud eight years after (their death), as if bidding farewell to the living and the dead, then he ascended the pulpit and said, ""I am your predecessor before you, and I am a witness on you, and your promised place to meet me will be Al- Haud (i.e. the Tank) (on the Day of Resurrection), and I am (now) looking at it from this place of mine. I am not afraid that you will worship others besides Allah, but I am afraid that worldly life will tempt you and cause you to compete with each other for it."" That was the last look which I cast on Allah's Messenger (ﷺ). ""1481"",Muhammad b. Sa'd reported on the authority of his father (Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas (Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had said:Tho month is thus and thus"""
1481,"[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: ""I am your predecessor at the Basin, and men from among you will be raised up, then they will be snatched away before me. So I will say: 'O my Lord, my companions!' And it will be said: 'You do not know what they introduced after you.'""
1482"""
1482,"Narrated Haritha bin Wahb: I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) mention Al-Hawd (the Reservoir), and he said: ""It is as (the distance) between Al-Madinah and Sana'a."""
1483,"[AI-translation] Al-Mustawrid said to him: ""Did you not hear it?"" Al-Awani said: ""No."" Al-Mustawrid said: ""In it are vessels like the stars.""
1484"""
1484,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar: The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""In front of you there is a lake as large as the distance between Jarba' and Adhruh."""
1485,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""O Unais! Go to the wife of this (man) and if she confesses (that she has committed illegal sexual intercourse), then stone her to death."""""""
1486,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, The Hour will not be established till a fire will come out of the land of Hijaz"""
1487,"Abu Huraira reported Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) as saying:A person visited his brother in another town and Allah deputed an Angel to wait for him on his way and when he came to him he said: Where do you intend to go? He said: I intend to go to my brother in this town. He said: Have you done any favour to him (the repayment of which you intend to get)? He said: No, excepting this that I love Mm for the sake of Allah, the Exalted and Glorious. Thereupon he said: I am a meesenger to you from, Allah: (to inform you) that Allah loves you as you love him (for His sake)"""
1488,"I saw Allah's Messenger.r- d- d,.uron the day of the battle of Uhud accompanied by twof men fighting on his behalf. They were dressed in white and were fighting withextreme bravery. I had nevseen them before, ndid I saw them laton. [(It is said that they were angel Jibrael (Gabriel) and angel Mik6'el (Michael)1. Courage of AllAh's MessengF: -!.r """
1489,"Narrated Anas:\n\nThe 'Prophet was the best and the bravest amongst the people. Once the people of Medina got terrified \nat night, so they went in the direction of the noise (that terrified them). The Prophet (ﷺ) met them (on his \nway back) after he had found out the truth. He was riding an unsaddled horse belonging to Abu Talha \nand a sword was hanging by his neck, and he was saying, \Don't be afraid! Don't be afraid!\"" He \nfurther said ""1490"",Anas b. Malik reported:We went out from Medina to Mecca with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he prayed two rak'ahs at each time of prayer till we returned to Medina. I said: For how long did he stay in Mecca? He said: (For) ten (days)"""
1490,"[AI-translation] Ibn 'Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, was the most generous of people, and he was at his most generous in Ramadan, when Jibril met him. He would meet him every night in Ramadan and study the Quran with him. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, was more generous with good than the blowing wind.""
1491"""
1491,"Narrated Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): I served the Prophet (ﷺ) for ten years, and he never said to me ""Uff"" (an expression of displeasure), nor did he ever say to me, ""Why did you do that?"" or ""Why did you not do that?"""
1492,"Jabir b. Abdullah (Allah be pleased with them) reported:Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) visited the orchard of Umm Ma'sud and said: Umm Ma'bad. he who has planted this tree, is he a Muslim or a non-Muslim? She said: Of course, he is a Muslim, whereupon he (the Holy Prophet) said: No Muslim who plants (trees) and from their fruits the human beings or the beasts or birds eat, but that would be taken as an act of charity on the Day of Resurrection"""
1493,"Narrated `Abdullah bin `Amr bin Al `Aas:\n\nAllah's Messenger (ﷺ) stopped (for a while near the Jimar) at Mina during his last Hajj for the people and \nthey were asking him questions. A man came and said, \I forgot and got my head shaved before \nslaughtering the Hadi (sacrificing animal).\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said"""
1494,"Once the Prophet (ﷺ) said (to me), If the money of Bahrain comes"""
1495,"We went with Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) (p.b.u.h) to the blacksmith Abu Saif, and he was the husband of the wet-nurse of Ibrahim (the son of the Prophet). Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) took Ibrahim and kissed him and smelled him and later we entered Abu Saif's house and at that time Ibrahim was in his last breaths, and the eyes of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) (p.b.u.h) started shedding tears. `Abdur Rahman bin `Auf said, ""O Allah's Apostle, even you are weeping!"" He said, ""O Ibn `Auf, this is mercy."" Then he wept more and said, ""The eyes are shedding tears and the heart is grieved, and we will not say except what pleases our Lord, O Ibrahim ! Indeed we are grieved by your separation."""""""
1496,"A bedouin came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said, ""You (people) kiss the boys! We don't kiss them."" The Prophet said, ""I cannot put mercy in your heart after Allah has taken it away from it."""""""
1497,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) kissed Al-Hasan bin `Ali while Al-Aqra' bin H`Abis at-Tamim was sitting beside him. Al-Aqra said, I have ten children and I have never kissed anyone of them"""
1498,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, He who is not merciful to others ""1499"",Narrated Abu Sa`id Al-Khudri:\n\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) was shier than a veiled virgin girl."""
1499,"[AI-translation] Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Prophet, peace be upon him, was more bashful than a virgin in her chamber.""
1500"""
1500,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr: The Prophet (ﷺ) was neither obscene nor did he seek obscenity. And he used to say: ""Indeed, among the best of you are those who have the best manners."""
1501,"Husain b. 'Abd al-Rahman reported:I was with Sa'id b. Jubair when he said: Who amongst you saw a star shooting last night? I said: It was I; then I said: I was in fact not (busy) in prayer, but was stung by a scorpion (and that is the reason why I was awake and had a glimpse of the shooting star). He said: Then what did you do? I said: I practised charm. He said: What urged you to do this? I said: (I did this according to the implied suggestion) of the hadith which al-Shu'ba narrated. He said: What did al-Shu'ba narrate to you? I said: Buraida b. Husaib al-Aslami narrated to us. The charm is of no avail except in case of the (evil influence) of an eye or the sting of a scorpion. He said: He who acted according to what he had heard (from the Holy Prophet) acted rightly, but Ibn 'Abbas narrated to us from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that he said: There were brought before me the peoples and I saw an apostle and a small group (of his followers) along with him, another (apostle) and one or two persons (along with him) and (still another) apostle having no one with him. When a very large group was brought to me I conceived as if it were my Ummah. Then it was said to me: It is Moses and his people. You should look at the horizon, and I saw a very huge group. It was again said to me: See the other side of the horizon, and there was (also) a very huge group. It was said to me: This is your Ummah, and amongst them there were seventy thousand persons who would be made to enter Paradise without rendering any account and without (suffering) any torment. He then stood up and went to his house. Then the people began to talk about the people who would be admitted to Paradise without rendering any account and without (suffering) any torment. Some of them said: They may be those who (have had the good fortune of living) in the company of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and some of them said: They be those who were born in Islam and did not associate anything with Allah. Some people mentioned other things. Thereupon came forth the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) before them and he said: What was that which you were talking about? They informed him. He said: They are those persons who neither practise charm, nor ask others to practise it, nor do they take omens, and repose their trust in their Lord. Upon this 'Ukkasha b. Mihsan stood up and said: Supplicate for me that He should make me one among them. Upon this he (Messenger of Allah) said: Thou are one among them. Then another man stood up and said: Supplicate before Allah that He should make me one among them. Upon this he said: 'Ukkisha has preceded you"""
1502,"Abu Huraira reported:I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying: The truest word which the poet stated is the word of Labid: Behold! apart from Allah everything is vain"""" ""1503"",Narrated Anas:\n\nI have never touched silk or Dibaj (i.e. thick silk) softer than the palm of the Prophet (ﷺ) nor have I smelt \na perfume nicer than the sweat of the Prophet."""
1503,"[AI-translation] Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I never touched silk or brocade softer than the palm of the Prophet, peace be upon him, nor have I ever smelled any scent or fragrance sweeter than the scent or fragrance of the Prophet, peace be upon him.""
1504"""
1504,"Narrated Anas (bin Malik): Umm Sulaim used to spread a leather sheet for the Prophet (ﷺ) and he would take his midday nap on that sheet at her house. He said: When the Prophet (ﷺ) slept, she would take some of his sweat and hair and collect it in a small bottle, and then she would gather it in some perfume."
1505,"(the mother of the faithful believers) Al-Harith bin Hisham asked Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) O Allah's Messenger (ﷺ)! How is the Divine Inspiration revealed to you?"" Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) replied"""
1506,"The PrOphet d- .rJ, ru . was of moderate height having broad shoulders, (long) hai reaching his ear-lobes. Once I saw him in a red cloak and I had nevseen a more handome person thand him ""1507"",Al-Bara' reported that Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) had the most handsome face amongst men and he had the best disposition and he was neither very tall nor short-statured"""
1507,"[AI-translation] Al-Bara' said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, was the most beautiful of people in face, and the best of them in character. He was neither exceedingly tall nor short.""
1508"""
1508,"Narrated Anas: The hair of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was wavy, neither straight nor curly, and it reached between his ears and his shoulders."
1509,"[AI-translation] Anas: that the hair of the Prophet, peace be upon him, used to reach his shoulders.""
1510"""
1510,"Narrated Muhammad bin Sirin: I asked Anas, ""Did the Prophet (ﷺ) dye his hair?"" He said, ""He did not reach old age (i.e., grey hair) except a little."""
1511,"[AI-translation] Suwa'i said: I saw the Prophet, peace be upon him, and I saw whiteness below his lower lip, the goatee.""
1512"""
1512,"Narrated Abu Juhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him): I saw the Prophet (ﷺ), and Al-Hasan bin 'Ali (peace be upon them both) resembled him."
1513,"Narrated As-Sa'ib bin Yazid: My aunt took me to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, my nephew is sick."" He wiped my head and prayed for blessing for me. Then he performed ablution (Wudu'), and I drank from the water of his ablution. Then I stood behind his back and looked at the seal of Prophethood between his shoulders, which was like a button of a tent."
1514,"Narrated Anas bin Malik, describing the Prophet (ﷺ): He was of medium height among the people, neither tall nor short. He was of a radiant (reddish-white) complexion, neither excessively white nor dark brown. His hair was neither curly nor straight. Revelation came to him when he was forty years old. He stayed in Makkah for ten years receiving revelation, and in Madinah for ten years. When he passed away, there were not twenty white hairs in his head and beard."
1515,"[AI-translation] Aishah: that the Prophet, peace be upon him, died at the age of sixty-three.""
1516"""
1516,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) remained in Makkah for thirteen years, and he died when he was sixty-three years old."
1517,"Narrated Jubair bin Mut'im (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""I have five names: I am Muhammad and Ahmad; and I am al-Mahi (the effacer) by whom Allah effaces disbelief; and I am al-Hashir (the gatherer) at whose feet the people will be gathered; and I am al-'Aqib (the one after whom there is no other Prophet)."""
1518,"The Prophet (ﷺ) did something and allowed his people to do it, but some people refrained from doing it. When the Prophet (ﷺ) learned of that, he delivered a sermon, and after having sent Praises to Allah, he said, ""What is wrong with such people as refrain from doing a thing that I do? By Allah, I know Allah better than they, and I am more afraid of Him than they."""""""
1519,"Az-Zubair told me that he quarreled with an Ansari man who had participated in (the battle of) Badr in front of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) about a water stream which both of them used for irrigation. Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said to Az-Zubair, O Zubair! Irrigate (your garden) first"""
1520,"An Ansari man quarreled with Az-Zubair in the presence of the Prophet (ﷺ) about the Harra Canals which were used for irrigating the date-palms. The Ansari man said to Az-Zubair, ""Let the water pass' but Az-Zubair refused to do so. So, the case was brought before the Prophet (ﷺ) who said to Az-Zubair, ""O Zubair! Irrigate (your land) and then let the water pass to your neighbor."" On that the Ansari got angry and said to the Prophet, ""Is it because he (i.e. Zubair) is your aunt's son?"" On that the color of the face of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) changed (because of anger) and he said, ""O Zubair! Irrigate (your land) and then withhold the water till it reaches the walls between the pits round the trees."" Zubair said, ""By Allah, I think that the following verse was revealed on this occasion"": ""But no, by your Lord They can have No faith Until they make you judge In all disputes between them."" (4.65)"""
1521,"That his father said, When `Umar was stabbed"""
1522,"Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) delivered a sermon the like of which I have never heard. He said: ""If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."" Thereupon, the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) covered their faces, weeping softly. A man asked: ""Who is my father?"" He replied: ""So-and-so."" Then this verse was revealed: ""Do not ask about things which, if they are shown to you, will distress you."""""""
1523,"Once the people started asking Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) questions, and they asked so many questions that he became angry and ascended the pulpit and said, ""I will answer whatever questions you may ask me today."" I looked right and left and saw everyone covering his face with his garment and weeping. Behold ! There was a man who, on quarreling with the people, used to be called as a son of a person other than h is father. He said, ""O Allah's Messenger (ﷺ)! Who is my father?"" The Prophet (ﷺ) replied, ""Your father is Hudhaifa."" And then `Umar got up and said, ""We accept Allah as our Lord, and Islam as (our) religion, and Muhammad as (our) Apostle; and we seek refuge with Allah from the afflictions."" Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, "" I have never seen a day like today in its good and its evil for Paradise and the Hell Fire were displayed in front of me, till I saw them just beyond this wall."" Qatada, when relating this Hadith, used to mention the following Verse:-- 'O you who believe! Ask not questions about things which, If made plain to you, May cause you trouble. (5.101)"""
1524,"The Prophet (ﷺ) was asked about things which he did not like, but when the questioners insisted, the Prophet got angry. He then said to the people, ""Ask me anything you like."" A man asked, ""Who is my father?"" The Prophet (ﷺ) replied, ""Your father is Hudhafa."" Then another man got up and said, ""Who is my father, O Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) ?"" He replied, ""Your father is Salim, Maula (the freed slave) of Shaiba."" So when `Umar saw that (the anger) on the face of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said, ""O Allah's Messenger (ﷺ)! We repent to Allah (Our offending you)."""
1525,"Abu Huraira said, ""The Prophet (ﷺ) said, 'A prayer performed in congregation is twenty-five times more superior in reward to a prayer performed by a single person. The angels of the night and the angels of the day are assembled at the time of the Fajr (Morning) prayer."" Abu Huraira added, ""If you wish, you can recite:-- 'Verily! The recitation of the Qur'an in the early dawn (Morning prayer) is ever witnessed (attended by the angels of the day and the night).' (17.78)"""
1526,"I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, Nothing is left of the prophetism except Al-Mubashshirat."" They asked"""
1527,"I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, Nothing is left of the prophetism except Al-Mubashshirat."" They asked"""
1528,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Allah created Adam in His picture ""1529"",Abu Huraira (Allah be pleased with him) reported:Prayer in the mosque of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) is more excellent than a thousand prayers in other mosques except the Masjid al-Haram"""
1529,"[AI-translation] Hadith of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Ibrahim, peace be upon him, was circumcised when he was eighty years old with an adze.""
1530"""
1530,"Narrated Abu Huraira (رضي الله عنه): The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""We have more right to be in doubt than Abraham when he said: 'My Lord! Show me how You give life to the dead.' Allah said: 'Do you not believe?' He said: 'Yes, but to be stronger in faith.' May Allah have mercy on Lot; he sought refuge with a strong support (i.e. Allah). And if I were to stay in prison as long as Joseph stayed, I would readily respond to the call (of the one who called me to get out of the prison)."""
1531,"Ibrdhim (Abraham) r:r.lr{ did not tell a liee except on three occasions. Twice fo the sake of Allah J-.# when he said, I am sick"""
1532,"Abu Huraira reported that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""The Children of Israel used to bathe naked, looking at one another. But Moses used to bathe alone. They said: 'By Allah, nothing prevents Moses from bathing with us except that he has a scrotal hernia.' So he went once to bathe, and placed his garment on a stone. The stone fled with his garment. Moses ran after it saying: 'My garment, O stone! My garment, O stone!' Until the Children of Israel saw Moses, and they said: 'By Allah, there is nothing wrong with Moses.' And he took his garment and began striking the stone with it. Abu Huraira said: 'By Allah, there are still six or seven marks on the stone from his striking.'"""""""
1533,"The angel of death was sent to Moses and when he went to him, Moses slapped him severely, spoiling one of his eyes. The angel went back to his Lord, and said, You sent me to a slave who does not want to die."" Allah restored his eye and said"""
1534,"Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: Two men reviled each other, a Muslim and a Jew. The Muslim said: ""By Him Who chose Muhammad over the worlds."" The Jew said: ""By Him Who chose Moses over the worlds."" At that, the Muslim raised his hand and slapped the Jew's face. The Jew went to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and informed him of what had happened between him and the Muslim. The Prophet (peace be upon him) called the Muslim and asked him about it, and he informed him. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Do not give me preference over Moses, for people will faint on the Day of Resurrection, and I will faint with them, and I will be the first to recover, and behold, Moses will be grasping the side of the Throne. So I do not know whether he was among those who fainted and recovered before me, or whether he was among those whom Allah exempted."""""""
1535,"While Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) was sitting, a Jew came and said, O Abul Qasim! One of your companions has slapped me on my face."" The Prophet (ﷺ) asked who that was. He replied that he was one of the Ansar. The Prophet (ﷺ) sent for him"""
1536,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Allah created Adam in His picture"""
1537,"Narrated Ibn `Abbas:\n\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) said, \One should not say that I am better than Jonah (i.e. Yunus) bin Matta.\"" So"""
1538,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him: It was said, ""O Messenger of Allah, who is the most honorable of people?"" He said, ""The most righteous of them."" They said, ""It is not about this we ask you."" He said, ""Then Yusuf, the Prophet of Allah, son of the Prophet of Allah, son of the Prophet of Allah, son of the Friend of Allah."" They said, ""It is not about this we ask you."" He said, ""Then you are asking about the roots of the Arabs? The best of them in the pre-Islamic period are the best of them in Islam when they acquire understanding."""""""
1539,"I said to Ibn `Abbas, Nauf-Al-Bakali claims that Moses (the companion of Khadir) was not the Moses of Bani Israel but he was another Moses."" Ibn `Abbas remarked that the enemy of Allah (Nauf) was a liar. Narrated Ubai bin Ka`b: The Prophet (ﷺ) said ""1540"",Hafsa (Allah be pleased with her) reported:I said to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ): What is the matter with people that they have put off Ihram"""
1540,"[AI-translation] Hadith of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I said to the Prophet, peace be upon him, while I was in the cave: If one of them were to look beneath his feet, he would see us. He said: What do you think, O Abu Bakr, of two, with Allah as their third?"""
